arget_id":"5d21-37ce-b5e4-4bf6"},{"link_uuid":"6b63ed9b-4ce1-4fce-ae01-ea4dca5c615a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"dc82-067b-1fd5-4f35"},{"link_uuid":"74109c31-d1c9-42b7-9865-b672bb0fcaba","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"bf36-a116-023f-4de6"},{"link_uuid":"8ccae5be-174a-41fa-8955-2cba69de76dc","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e945-1ef6-45f1-46c9"},{"link_uuid":"72b6d90e-4717-40bd-91b4-6b1853647e4e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0e21-f211-2026-4266"},{"link_uuid":"c3347256-6b0c-4078-8cf9-68e4d974259a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b4c8-ad90-a6f3-4f03"},{"link_uuid":"561d41ac-8d62-4fdd-ae16-337d5c58af1a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5929-9076-bed2-4aca"},{"link_uuid":"ed1ede78-ea5e-479e-8233-5e37a0d809fe","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1a36-6a56-3196-49c6"},{"link_uuid":"374479da-762b-4800-a9e7-bd19373cdebc","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5598-c599-4979-4f0a"},{"link_uuid":"5daee64e-67fb-4e06-91f3-72d80fedebf4","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a1ad-7021-f61b-4870"},{"link_uuid":"b5f43ce2-981e-4292-9601-bde36e7b1b92","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8329-0d5f-4571-4758"},{"link_uuid":"9b7c5dce-9ad3-4bf4-a1f0-162ecf766c0f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"3d43-762a-d149-4b80"},{"link_uuid":"3c4eabfd-3d94-479e-ae7e-f27c0f33757a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0e6a-c785-ec27-4ec7"},{"link_uuid":"e3c0612f-266a-40cc-989e-a4f386e6f40d","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"fc7b-ed6f-2f29-41d6"},{"link_uuid":"63bcb9e9-386d-4cba-9877-a2b7054d402c","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c885-1f3d-be32-416e"},{"link_uuid":"5bb3ddb4-cf91-4149-a50e-fa50687c0f01","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"058e-56fb-6ac7-4d12"},{"link_uuid":"fd1a1d73-5c4c-4c4d-987d-a21a1f85a05e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ff13-a19a-f610-49bb"},{"link_uuid":"c3f1720d-3a20-40d2-9c97-ee0e42cd2d19","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a97b-b4af-08c1-40ae"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/_bank_observer.py:1-34, 49-60, 83-96, 124-134` — Preserve banking-event definitions, signature fidelity, evidence-count semantics, and bounded-gap oracle. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/_child_diag.py:56-84, 97-118` — Preserve return-code-first checking, signal handling, and stderr-tail diagnostics. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/_extra_guard.py:1-23` — Preserve lean-install skip versus full-lane hard-failure contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/_git_counts.py:1-13` — Preserve retry conditions and diagnostic-preserving terminal error. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/_git_floor.py:1-16` — Preserve Git 2.38 requirement and fail-loud policy. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/_git_upkeep.py:1-46` — Preserve detached-maintenance hazard, required bare-remote pins, and trace-based oracle. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/_isolation.py:22-29, 33-46, 122-131, 145-156, 176-184` — Preserve watched paths, bounded re-sampling, non-attribution limitation, and report-only safety. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/_jira_shape_contract.py:1-19` — Preserve the shared real/fake return-shape contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/_live_jira_confinement.py:1-23` — Preserve that `xdist_group` is effective only with `loadgroup`. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/_log_integrity.py:1-44, 104-113` — Preserve fail-open `caplog` hazard and per-test logger-level restoration. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/_nested_pytest.py:1-15, 46-61` — Preserve owned `--basetemp`, explicit environment forwarding, timeout, and cache isolation. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/_repo_root.py:1-21` — Preserve install-agnostic checkout discovery and failure behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/_stall_remote.py:1-12` — Preserve stall/dribble semantics and cleanup obligation. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/_subprocess_isolation.py:1-28` — Preserve isolation escape definition, AST guard scope, and mandatory opt-out reason. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/_topology_template.py:212-226` — Preserve refusal to copy while detached upkeep may be active. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/_tree_scan.py:1-10` — Preserve one immutable cached AST parse per resolved root. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/conftest.py:1-20, 137-143, 149-156, 196-205, 229-245, 272-282, 289-298, 388-400, 404-410, 444-457, 504-515, 538-550, 556-579, 587-597, 619-632, 639-656, 739-755, 779-814` — Preserve current isolation, tiering, environment-scrubbing, process, and logging contracts; single-source their rationale in the owning helpers. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/module_size_support.py:1-18` — Preserve single-source `wc -l` semantics, import stability, and the two consumers. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/_bank_observer.py tests/_child_diag.py tests/_extra_guard.py tests/_git_counts.py tests/_git_floor.py tests/_git_upkeep.py tests/_isolation.py tests/_jira_shape_contract.py tests/_live_jira_confinement.py tests/_log_integrity.py tests/_nested_pytest.py tests/_repo_root.py tests/_stall_remote.py tests/_subprocess_isolation.py tests/_topology_template.py tests/_tree_scan.py tests/conftest.py tests/module_size_support.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/_bank_observer.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/_child_diag.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/_extra_guard.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/_git_counts.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/_git_floor.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/_git_upkeep.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/_isolation.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/_jira_shape_contract.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/_live_jira_confinement.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/_log_integrity.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/_nested_pytest.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/_repo_root.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/_stall_remote.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings